# Git workflow

## Branches (canonical)

- `main` — production. Protected. No agent commits or pushes. No `feature/*` → `main`.
- `test` — integration / QA. Feature work merges here first.
- `release/<rel-id>` — cut from `test`. Merged into `main` only by a human.
- `feature/<feature-id>-<description>` — implementation **only after `PLANNED`**
- `bugfix/<bug-id>-<description>` — fixes
- `docs/<description>` — documentation only
- `chore/<description>` — maintenance
- `cursor/<description>-<id>` — compatibility alias for Cursor cloud branches.
  Treat as `feature/` or `release/` by purpose. Prefer canonical names in new docs.

Work only on those branch types. Never commit on `main`. Never push to `main`.

## Pull requests

- Implementation PRs target `test`
- Release PRs are `release/<rel-id>` → `main` and require **human** merge
- Do not merge PRs to `main`
- Do not approve your own human-required gates

## Release → test (mechanical)

After a human merges `release/<rel-id>` → `main`:

1. GitHub Actions (`.github/workflows/release-sync.yml`) merges the
   **release branch** into `test` (not `main` into `test`).
2. Agent fallback if Actions cannot (Ask mode cannot push).
3. Delete `release/<rel-id>` **only if** that sync succeeded.
4. Do not treat this as product QA. A PR to `test` is only for
   protection rejection.

If the merge into `test` fails, stop. Don't force it, don't delete the
branch. Record the failure.

Keep GitHub “delete branch on merge” **disabled** for release PRs.

Merged to `main` is lifecycle `ON_MAIN`, not `RELEASED`. See
`docs/sdlc/lifecycle.md`.

## Commits

Conventional Commits with work item ID when present:
feat(AUTH-001): implement user login
test(AUTH-001): add login e2e tests
fix(AUTH-001): handle invalid credentials
docs(AUTH-001): add login test plan

## Push

Push only when the human asks to push or prepare/update a PR. Never push
to `main`. Exceptions (no extra prompt):

- release→test sync and release-branch deletion — Actions or Agent
  fallback, no extra product approval
- CI **Prettier** (`format:check`) FAIL on a PR branch this agent
  owns: format locally, commit, push **that branch** so a new SHA
  re-runs CI. Never push `main` or `test` for this.
